Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
MIME-Version: 1.0

Late summer in the Midwest can bring sudden thunderstorms, hail, and high win=
ds. A little prep now can save a lot of trouble later.

1. Clear gutters and downspouts so water flows away from your foundation.
2. Trim dead or overhanging branches near your roof and power lines.
3. Test your sump pump by pouring a bucket of water into the pit.
4. Secure patio furniture, grills, and trampolines before a storm rolls in.
5. Photograph your belongings and keep the files somewhere safe. It makes any=
 future claim much easier.

More seasonal tips: greatplainsmutual.example/safety

Stay safe,
